# Live sites and real companies only

Never send Stephan a link, company, or contact that has not been live-checked in this turn. Search hits, old notes, canvases, and sibling TLDs do not count.

## Check the exact URL you will send

GET it with a browser User-Agent. Follow redirects. Read the body.

HTTP 200 is not live. Drop it if any of these are true:

- Empty or near-empty body (WJA `.org` returned 200 with 114 bytes and no title)
- Parked, for-sale, coming-soon, or registrar placeholder
- Parking DNS (GoDaddy `3.33.130.190` / `15.197.148.33`, `wpdns.site`)
- Redirect to a malware or safebrowse warning (Retail Minded)
- Login wall or 403 on the only public page

Checking `example.com` does not make `example.org` live. Send only the URL that passed.

## The company must still exist

Need recent 2025/2026 content, events, or independent press on that live site. A Google MX record is not a mailbox. A directory listing is not a business.

## Contact must be published there

Use a mailto or working form on the live page. Never guess `hello@`, never reuse an email from a dead domain, never invent a URL.

## If it fails

Do not send the link. Say it is dead and drop it. Do not pad the list with a stretch replacement.
